    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the cornerstone of our lineup. His elite 81.26 score is the clear standout, driven by a favorable matchup against Dobbins and a massive +14% platoon adjustment that leverages his sprint speed in a high-efficiency environment. Alongside him, **Yordan Alvarez** (65.52) and **Junior Caminero** (62.27) anchor the heart of the order; despite facing formidable arms like Bryan Woo and Rogers, their elite xwOBA metrics allow them to transcend standard SP skill penalties. **Kyle Schwarber** (60.40) also earns a strong start, with his lead-off role against Kremer providing the necessary OBP runway to bolster our Roto categories.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Caleb Durbin** on the bench. With a 48.55 score, he sat just shy of our rotation requirements, falling behind **Pedro Ramirez** and **Gary Sanchez** due to a projected defensive struggle against the catcher's pop time. While **Caleb Durbin** offers high-upside speed, the model favored the higher baseline efficiency of our current starters. We are also keeping a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Yordan Alvarez** and **Nelson Velazquez**; should the actual order shift against our assumptions, their point totals will fluctuate significantly.\n\nRisk mitigation remains the theme for the bottom of our lineup. We are avoiding the sub-40 floor of **Chase Meidroth** and **Dillon Dingler** to protect our limited game caps, as their matchups against strong arms like Anderson and Burke present too much volatility for minimal category gain. Meanwhile, **Gary Sanchez** carries a warning flag due to facing Skubal\u2019s 2.77 xERA; he remains in the lineup purely as a volume play, though he is the most likely candidate to be pulled if we find ourselves ahead in HR/RBI early in the day.",
